    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation says the encoder creates the dense feature field, and windowing partitions that field while retaining its tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field named F. The window operator then partitions that field into X, keeping every token for later updates. This equation defines the carrier that the compact thought process reads and changes.",
